[
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# FIXED DEFECT, 2026-08-12, found by a judge in panel 034 while compiling something", "line": 1, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# else. Symptom: `heroes test examples/calculator/lex.hero` answered `panic: 1 heap", "line": 2, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# blocks still live at exit (a missing decref)` and failed a test that PASSED when the", "line": 3, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# same module was compiled as part of a larger program — byte-identical source, four", "line": 4, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# roots, one of them wrong.", "line": 5, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 6, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Cause, and it is the sharp part: `emit/perfn.rs::owns_case` asked the type interner", "line": 7, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# whether a variant case's payload owns a reference. `Ty::Case(decl, case)` is interned", "line": 8, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# when a `match` arm BINDS the payload — not when the case is built. So a module that", "line": 9, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# constructs `.name(s: …)` and never destructures it emitted", "line": 10, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 11, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#     void h_lex_Token_release(h_lex_Token *v) { switch (v->tag) { default: break; } }", "line": 12, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 13, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# an empty switch, while the very same declaration compiled beside a module holding the", "line": 14, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `match` emitted the walking release. The retain was always emitted, so every copy", "line": 15, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# increfed and nothing decrefed. Fix: `case_fields_are_counted` asks the FIELDS, which", "line": 16, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# do not move between compilations, where the interner does.", "line": 17, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 18, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# This program is that shape with nothing else in it: a case payload that owns a `str`,", "line": 19, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# built and copied and never matched on. The `str` must be computed — a literal is a", "line": 20, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# static block and cannot leak, which is why the corpus had 90 run cases and not one of", "line": 21, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# them met this.", "line": 22, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 23, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# What makes it a test rather than an anecdote is the leak counter in the shim: exit 0", "line": 24, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# and correct output prove nothing here, because the defect produced both.", "line": 25, "col": 1},
